{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>You shall not pervert the judgment of your poor.</b> Perhaps HaShem commanded concerning the judgment of the poor, after the manner of the statement of the Sages, may their memory be for blessing (Bava Metzia 71a): ״Your poor and the poor of your city, etc. — the poor of your city and the poor of another city — the poor of your city take precedence.״ Therefore the commandment comes here in the form of a prohibition, not to pervert the judgment of the one who is first [in precedence] in favor of the one who comes after, and that is what the verse says: ״your poor״ — [meaning, your poor first]."], :book :exodus, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 23, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:32:41.559286282Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}